semgrep ci `--no-suppress-errors` now exits with code 2 (instead of 0) when dependency resolution fails for a subproject while local builds are allowed (--allow-local-builds): a build or package manager command fails, a lockfile cannot be parsed at all, or a build succeeds but reports an incomplete dependency list (for example, a registry refused a request). The affected dependency sources are listed in the scan output and the scan no longer reports that it completed successfully. Findings from the other subprojects are still reported. The default behavior, where errors are suppressed, is unchanged, and so is any scan without --allow-local-builds. Semgrep Managed Scanning scans are not affected.
